# API Surface and Docs Truth

## Management API

- All REST endpoints live under `/mgmt/*` in `teamserver/internal/server/management.go`.
- Before adding a client call (CLI in `client/cli/`, MCP in `mcp/grpc_client.py`), verify the route exists there. Do not invent endpoints.
- CLI and MCP must use identical endpoint paths and JSON field names (e.g. kill uses `{"id": ...}`).
- Task payloads use numeric `TaskType` values from `teamserver/proto/tasks.proto`.

## Docs truth

If a change implements or removes a capability, update in the same change:

- `README.md` (user-facing behavior, Known Limitations)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (component claims)
- `docs/OPERATOR_GUIDE.md` (commands and endpoints)
- `CHANGELOG.md` (user-visible changes)

Never document aspirational features as existing. Verify documented commands exist before writing them into guides.

## Examples

```bash
# BAD: adding a client call to an endpoint that does not exist
mgmtPost("/mgmt/pivots/add", ...)   # route is /mgmt/pivots/socks/start or /mgmt/pivots/portfwd

# GOOD: match the server route
mgmtPost("/mgmt/build/implant", ...)

# BAD: regex that silently drops task names with digits
re.compile(r"(TASK_[A-Z_]+)")

# GOOD
re.compile(r"(TASK_[A-Z0-9_]+)")
```